# No live-tree edits

`H:\PropORACLE_main_cp` is the scheduled-task checkout. Do not edit files there, restore them with `git checkout`, or `git pull` over dirty files without a saved diff.

**Every change goes through origin/main, then a pull on the live tree.** That is how work stays in one place.

Before any `git checkout --`, `git restore`, `git reset`, or overwrite of a live-tree file:

1. `git -C H:\PropORACLE_main_cp diff -- <paths> > backups/live_dirty_<yyyyMMdd_HHmmss>.patch`
2. Only then restore or pull.
3. Keep the patch. Do not delete it after the restore.

If a live file is dirty and you need it to match main, save the patch first even when you think the dirt is junk. Today’s discarded six-script restore lost uncommitted mixer-hold wiring because no patch was saved.
